entry.summary:
In React, props (short for properties) allow you to pass data from a parent component to a child component. It’s one of the most important concepts that makes components reusable and dynamic. 👉 Example: function Welcome(props) {
Used like this: <Welcome name="Aman" /> 📌 Key points: 💡 Bonus tip: Use destructuring for cleaner code function Welcome({ name }) {
Mastering props is your first step toward building clean and scalable React apps.
